## 🛠️ Testing Instructions

### Step 1: Install Arduino Libraries
Before you flash the updated code, ensure you have the **Adafruit Fingerprint Sensor Library** installed in your Arduino IDE (Sketch > Include Library > Manage Libraries).

### Step 2: Restart Your Stack
1. Restart your **Node.js API** so it registers the new `POST /vehicles/:id/enroll` route.
2. Hot Restart (`r`) your **Flutter App**.

### Step 3: Trigger an Enrollment
1. Open the Flutter app, go to **Fleet**, and tap your vehicle to open the details.
2. Tap the **Driver Auth** button.
3. Tap **Enroll New Fingerprint**. You will see a success snackbar confirming the API sent the command.
4. On your ESP32 serial monitor, you will see it enter Enrollment Mode. Place a finger on the sensor, wait for it to say "Remove finger", and then place it again to complete the enrollment!
